and with all vacancies which shall from time to time exist to be filled for the unexpired term thereof by the respective governing authority which selected the member whose position shall become vacant.
Members shall, notwithstanding their terms of office, serve at the pleasure of the governing authority which selected each such member and each member shall be subject to removal prior to the termination of his or her term by action of the governing authority which so selected such member.
Upon selection and commencement of his or her term, each member shall serve [subject to death or resignation and subject to removal] until both the selection of and the commencement of the term of his or her successor.

757:
A member of the commission who:
(1) Has a property interest in any real property affected by any proposed rezoning action pending before the commission;
(2) Has a financial interest in any business entity which has a property interest in any real property affected by any proposed rezoning action pending before the commission; or
(3) Has a member of the family who has any interest described in either paragraph (1) or paragraph (2) of this section;
shall at or prior to the initial meeting of the commission at which the matter is to be considered disclose the nature and extent of such interest in writing to the applicant and to the commission. All such disclosures shall be entered into the minutes of meetings of the commission [but in no event later than immediately following the announcement of the matter for consideration by the commission], shall be matters of public record of both the commission and the governmental entity involved and shall be available for public inspection at any time during normal working hours.

761:
The commission shall function only in an advisory capacity to each of the respective governing authorities. In connection therewith, the commission shall [subject to the direction, control, and instructions of the respective governing authority of each governmental entity] conduct surveys and studies of existing conditions and probably future developments and shall develop plans for physical, social, and economic growth which will best promote the public health, safety, morals, convenience, prosperity, general welfare, efficiency, and economy in the development of the governmental entity involved and submit the same to the governing authority of each governmental entity, and shall also [subject to the direction, control, and instructions of the respective governing authority of each governmental entity]:
(a) Develop and submit to the governing authority of each governmental entity for its consideration of a master plan, and amendments thereto, for the development of each governmental entity;
(b) Develop and submit to the governing authority of each governmental entity for its consideration recommendations relative to amendments to or revisions of the zoning ordinance and zoning maps of the governmental entity;
(c) Review proposed amendments to or revisions of the zoning ordinances and zoning maps of each of the respective governmental entities which shall be submitted by others, make findings with respect thereto, and make recommendations to the governing authority of the governmental entity involved with respect to the adoption, rejection, modification, or conditional adoption of each such proposed amendment or revision;
(d) Develop and submit to the governing authority of each governmental entity for its consideration regulations and amendments thereto for the subdivision of land;
(e) Develop and submit to the governing authority of each governmental entity for its consideration official maps or plats, and amendments thereto, which designate the exact location of the boundary lines of existing, proposed, extended, widened and narrowed streets, public ways, public open spaces, and public buildings and sites together with regulations and amendments thereto for the erection of buildings and other structures to be located therein; and
(f) Perform such additional functions and services for and on behalf of each governmental entity as shall be authorized or directed from time to time by the governing authority thereof.

765:
The respective secretaries of the commission shall provide administrative assistance to the commission relative to matters relating to each of their respective governmental entities and specifically shall with respect to matters which are relative to their respective governmental entities:
(a) Prepare and conduct all correspondence of the commission;
(b) Receive and file all correspondence to the commission;
(c) Receive and file all applications and filings to and with the commission;
(d) Receive and file all transmittals to the commission from the zoning administrator of the governmental entity and other public officials;
(e) Review and evaluate all applications and filings to and with the commission for compliance with the rules and regulations of the commission and notify those filing the same of any noncompliance therewith;
(f) Following consultation with the chairman [and to the extent necessary the other members] schedule meetings of the commission in accordance with applicable law, ordinances, resolutions, and the rules and regulations of the commission;
(g) Prepare and maintain a calendar and docket of proposed rezoning actions before the commission;
(h) Prepare and submit to the members at least 24 hours prior to a scheduled hearing an agenda therefore as well as copies of all applications and other filings made in connection with each such proceeding;
(i) Determine all notices to be given in connection with proceedings before the commission and cause such notices to be given to those entitled thereto;
(j) Attend all meetings and hearings of the commission;
(k) Cause a mechanical record to be made of all meetings and hearings of the commission relative to proposed rezoning actions by use of tape recorder or other appropriate device;
(l) Cause to be retained and maintained a copy or a facsimile of all physical evidence presented in connection with proposed rezoning actions;
(m) Prepare and maintain minutes of proceedings of the commission indicating therein all significant information, matters, and facts pertaining thereto including specifically all motions, votes, and decisions of the commission together with the vote of each member upon each such motion, vote, and decision including those absent, disqualified, or failing to vote thereon together with such other matters as shall be pertinent to the activities of the commission;
(n) Cause to be retained and maintained all minutes, records, files, and notices of the commission;
(o) At hearings of the commission with respect to proposed rezoning actions attempt to obtain the name and address of all persons who shall present any evidence, testimony, or opinions, make any statement to the commission, or present any argument in connection with the matter before the commission; and
(p) Perform such other duties as shall be directed from time to time by the commission which is approved by the chief administrative official of the governmental entity.

788:
Compliance with the provisions of this chapter shall not excuse or relieve any person from complying with the requirements and provisions of all other laws, ordinances, resolutions, rules and regulations applicable to animals and birds or to the conduct of any activity, business, trade, profession or occupation. Those additional laws, ordinances, rules and regulations include, but are not limited to:
(1) All applicable federal and state laws, rules and regulations;
(2) The business, occupational and professional license and permit requirements of the County/City;
(3) The obtaining of and compliance with business, occupational, trade and professional licenses and permits from the County/City as well as, to the extent applicable, the State and the United States;
(4) Compliance with the zoning ordinance of the County/City; and
(5) Compliance with all other applicable ordinances and resolutions of the County/City.

812:
No owner or custodian of any animal or bird shall fail to provide the animal or bird:
(1) With humane care;
(2) With adequate food and water;
(3) With adequate sanitary shelter which has adequate ventilation; or
